+## Provider API keys
+
+Open the app, enter keys in `Provider API keys`, and tap `Save keys`.
+
+Keys are stored locally in AsyncStorage and are not included in the export archive.
+
+## Cloud live mode
+
+Cloud live mode streams mono PCM16 chunks directly to provider WebSockets.
+
+First-build live audio sources:
+
+- `expo-audio-stream`: official `expo-audio` `useAudioStream` hook, `int16` `ArrayBuffer` chunks.
+- `dr-pogodin-audio`: `@dr.pogodin/react-native-audio` `InputAudioStream`, `Buffer` chunks, explicit stream lifecycle and error listeners.
+
+Provider formats:
+
+- OpenAI: 24 kHz PCM, `gpt-realtime-whisper`.
+- ElevenLabs: 16 kHz PCM, `scribe_v2_realtime`.
+- Deepgram: 16 kHz linear16, `nova-3`.
+
+Both sources request the provider's target sample rate directly. The Expo source reports the actual sample rate per chunk; if a device refuses 16 kHz or 24 kHz, use the logs/results to spot it before judging provider quality.
+
+Because this uses native modules, rebuild the development app after installing dependencies or prebuilding.
+
+## Other live audio options
+
+These are documented for later experiments, but are not wired into the first build:
+
+- `@picovoice/react-native-voice-processor`: focused raw PCM frame capture for voice/VAD/STT, simple singleton API, good candidate if Expo/Dr Pogodin behave poorly on a device.
+- `react-native-waveform-recorder`: best if voice-note UX, waveform, pause/resume, preview, file backup, silence detection, and optional PCM stream become important. Heavier than needed for pure STT-live.
+- `@siteed/audio-studio`: broad Expo/RN audio toolkit with recording, streaming, analysis, visualization, VAD-style features, and more surface area than this prototype currently needs.
+- `react-native-audio-api`: powerful Web Audio-style graph/data callback approach; likely more useful for advanced processing/resampling than first-pass provider comparison.
+
+## Export
+
+Tap `Export data` to create a zip under:
+
+```text
+DocumentDirectory/voice-lab/exports/
+```
+
+The archive includes `notes.json`, result JSON files, and audio files for runs where audio was persisted. API keys are excluded.
+
 ## Whisper models

 For Russian, use multilingual models, not `.en` models.
